  "player_hint_1_en": "Only one square fits Celeste's clue (\"She was beside some flowers and a statue.\"). So Celeste (C) must be at row 6, column 2. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_2_en": "With the rows and columns of Celeste crossed out, only one square is left for Ezra that fits his clue (\"He was sitting in a chair in the Vicarage.\"). So Ezra (E) must be at row 3, column 3. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_3_en": "Horace is now the only person who can still go in row 9. So Horace (H) must be at row 9, column 5. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_4_en": "Barnaby can't be at row 1, column 1; row 2, column 1: in each case Victor would have nowhere left to go. Suppose Barnaby were at row 7, column 1: then Gideon would have nowhere left to go. So Barnaby can't be there. Testing the remaining squares the same way rules out a few more. So Barnaby (B) must be at row 5, column 1. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_5_en": "Suppose Dora were at row 1, column 4: then Victor would have nowhere left to go. So Dora can't be there. So Dora (D) must be at row 2, column 4. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_6_en": "Freya is now the only person who can still go in row 1. So Freya (F) must be at row 1, column 8. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_7_en": "The victim must share an area with exactly one other person. So Amber (A) must be at row 8, column 6. Cross out her row and column.",
  "player_hint_8_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Victor. So Victor (the victim) must be at row 4, column 9. Cross out his row and column.",
  "player_hint_9_en": "With the rows and columns of everyone placed so far crossed out, only one square is left for Gideon that fits his clue (\"He was exactly one row north of Amber.\"). So Gideon (G) must be at row 7, column 7. Cross out his row and column. Gideon is the only person in the Bell Tower with Victor, so Gideon is the murderer!"
